      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}\\cos(x),$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=3^{x} \\ln{\\left(3 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\cos(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =({3}^{x})^{\u2032}\\cos(x)+{3}^{x}(\\cos(x))^{\u2032} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\ln (3))\\cos(x)+{3}^{x}(-\\sin(x)) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\ln (3)\\cos(x)-{3}^{x}\\sin(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
